From 05fbb71c8a614cc12844d70f4965e67430e0f690 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:33:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [RetroPlayer] Browse video filters by category

With the shader presets add-on installed there are over a hundred video
filters, all in one row, which is a lot to scroll through to compare two
CRT shaders.

Skins can now add a category list (control 10813) above the filters. Its
categories are the presets' folders, after a "Built-in" one for the
scaling methods, and the filter row only shows the focused category.
Moving along the categories doesn't change the filter being used; going
into one applies its highlighted filter. Skins without the list still
get every filter in one row.

Right from a category's last filter goes on to the next category's
first, and Left from its first back to the previous category's last,
with the category list following, so every filter can still be reached
in one row. The last category leads back round to the first. The window
property "categorymove" says which way the row moved, so a skin can
slide the new filters in from that side.

Estuary gets the category row, with the category in use highlighted
while the filters have focus.
